# Default deny: only files explicitly re-included below reach Docker build.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!alembic.ini
!alembic/
!alembic/**
!src/
!src/**
!web/
!web/app/
!web/app/**

# Never include generated bytecode: .pyc files are rebuildable, carry absolute
# host paths in tracebacks, and would ship a second copy of any literal the
# source already contains (the Step 45 image scan found them).
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Never include generated frontend files or dependency trees.
web/app/node_modules/
web/app/dist/
web/app/tests/

# Defense in depth for sensitive or non-publishable runtime material.
.env*
**/.env*
secrets/
data/traces/
data/eval/reports/
data/eval/traces/
data/sessions/
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.wal
*.vec
*.key
*.pem
uploads/
exports/
backups/
tests/
.git/
.venv/
_venv/

# Retrieval data must ship in the image, or every agentic run dies on assembly:
# _load_fixture_clauses reads data/fixtures/, the version registry reads
# data/versions.json, and without data/indexes/ the retriever silently answers
# from a 2 KB fixture instead of the corpus.  These re-includes come LAST on
# purpose: .dockerignore resolves by last match, and *.db / *.vec / *.wal above
# would otherwise strip the index apart file by file.
#
# The index is treated as a versioned build artifact, not a runtime mount: it is
# produced by scripts/build_index.py (which needs DASHSCOPE_API_KEY and so must
# never run inside docker build) and then COPYed in, so a given image tag always
# retrieves from a known corpus with no operator setup step.  It is served with
# access_mode="read_only", which is what lets it live on the read-only root
# filesystem -- see TriviumRetriever.  Ship the directory whole: .lock and
# .flush_ok are required to open it, and .text/.text.meta are required for the
# hybrid text component (without them retrieval degrades to pure vector).
#
# data/eval/reports/, data/traces/ and data/sessions/ stay denied above; nothing
# here re-includes them (scripts/check_image.sh asserts the first is absent).
!data/
!data/fixtures/
!data/fixtures/**
!data/curated/
!data/curated/**
!data/versions.json
!data/indexes/
!data/indexes/**

# `!data/` above is needed so the build context descends into data/, but Docker
# counts a matching parent as matching its children -- which silently revives
# every deny further up (measured: traces/, sessions/, eval/reports/ and the
# 160 MB drawings/ all landed in the image).  So re-deny the rest of data/ HERE,
# after the re-includes, because last match wins.  Keep this list in sync when
# a new data/ subdirectory appears: the default is "does not ship".
data/eval/
data/traces/
data/sessions/
data/quality/
data/drawings/
data/mcp_servers.json
data/mcp_servers.example.json
**/.DS_Store
